 17592186045417 true] [17592186424189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424184 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424185 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424186 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424187 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424188 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424189 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424189 1077 "selection" 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424189 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424188 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424189 1079 #uuid "a9f1a53d-9e00-54ab-b914-f5c8b1d4efa0" 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424190 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424189 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424190 1069 "q-122737" 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424190 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424190 1071 "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=(x-y)^{2}?$" 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424190 1072 #uuid "6d9aa2a3-1ea1-5a5e-9577-ca5789b6206d" 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424190 1074 "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x-y)^{2}) \\\\  & =2(x-y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x-y)^{2}) \\\\  & =-2(x-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =2(x-y)\\,i-2(x-y)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(2,1),$ $(1,2),$ and $(1,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(2,1) & =2\\cdot (2-1)\\,i-2\\cdot (2-1)\\,j=2\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,2) & =2\\cdot (1-2)\\,i-2\\cdot (1-2)\\,j=-2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,-1) & =2\\cdot (1-(-1))\\,i-2\\cdot (1-(-1))\\,j=4\\,i-4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/96/96851fd456d3b9f0a6af941a255926f35e29bbe778ed05556af3f69145e38ef2.png)" 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424191 1058 #edb/ref 17592186424195 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424191 1062 #uuid "067003af-5c9a-5cbe-8472-bab19e50bc36" 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424191 1063 #edb/ref 17592186424190 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424192 1058 #edb/ref 17592186424194 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424192 1062 #uuid "6dfb476d-54a7-53df-8507-c3f88ca01082" 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424192 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179973 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424193 1058 #edb/ref 17592186424191 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424193 1062 #uuid "95442878-a2e5-5bfd-9abb-51c25d61cfe4" 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424193 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179967 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424194 1062 #uuid "99216207-5767-5618-bf28-eb5a98073708" 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424194 1063 #edb/ref 17592186387311 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424195 1058 #edb/ref 17592186424192 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424195 1062 #uuid "fe7b4648-c351-5000-80e4-1e9d858043ac" 13194139534524 17592186045417 true] [17592186424195 1063 #edb/ref 17592186256708 13194139534524 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-a15d5bb3-e629-5239-97bb-a068e0cf6a5b" 17592186424183 "answer-0afc3cbd-80cd-5f79-95d1-b02b58d14af7" 17592186424184 "answer-25ed12c7-2e43-5b16-b2e3-173b3c5367b8" 17592186424185 "answer-99f6e268-33a9-5e9a-a609-e6ee2c4c38d7" 17592186424186 "answer-c5dba748-9027-5a4a-bf33-0feb67920158" 17592186424187 "answer-cad5833b-0aa5-5948-b9b9-b322bb2fcf7b" 17592186424188 "answe